<title>UK: Zeneca falls as bid hopes fade.</title>
<headline>Zeneca falls as bid hopes fade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Zeneca Group Plc fell 26-1/2 pence to 18.06-1/2 stg as hopes of a bid from Swiss rival Roche Holding AG faded, dealers said.</p>
<p>Roche, frequently touted as eyeing Zeneca, reported its first-quarter sales results earlier on Tuesday, but made no mention of any bid intentions.</p>
<p>Zeneca shares shot up last week on a bid hope revival.</p>
<p>Zeneca was also still hurt by Monday's comments from ABN AMRO Hoare Govett, which said the shares looked expensive as they carried a bid premium between two and three stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
